Feature: Update Sales KPI Logic and Output for LifeScience Sales Pipeline

  Background:
    Given the existing PySpark pipeline for sales KPI calculation
    And the following requirements for logic updates:
      | Logic Item           | Requirement                                                                 |
      |---------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
      | Bonus Eligibility   | 'Yes' if sales_amount > 25000, else retain previous logic                   |
      | Performance Flag    | High if sales_amount > 9000, Medium if >7000 and <=9000, else Low           |
      | Product Perf Band   | Excellent if >10000, Good if >8000, Moderate if >5000, else Poor            |
      | Rep Tier            | Platinum Plus if total_sales_amount > 45000, Platinum if >35000, Gold if >25000, Silver otherwise |
    And the final output must display the updated DataFrames

  Scenario Outline: Validate performance_flag logic for sales transactions
    Given a sales transaction with sales_amount <sales_amount>
    When the pipeline calculates performance_flag
    Then the performance_flag should be "<expected_flag>"

    Examples:
      | sales_amount | expected_flag |
      | 9500         | High          |
      | 9000         | Medium        |
      | 8000         | Medium        |
      | 7001         | Medium        |
      | 7000         | Low           |
      | 5000         | Low           |
      | 0            | Low           |

  Scenario Outline: Validate product_perf_band logic for sales transactions
    Given a sales transaction with sales_amount <sales_amount>
    When the pipeline calculates product_perf_band
    Then the product_perf_band should be "<expected_band>"

    Examples:
      | sales_amount | expected_band |
      | 15000        | Excellent     |
      | 10001        | Excellent     |
      | 10000        | Good          |
      | 9000         | Good          |
      | 8001         | Good          |
      | 8000         | Moderate      |
      | 6000         | Moderate      |
      | 5001         | Moderate      |
      | 5000         | Poor          |
      | 1000         | Poor          |

  Scenario Outline: Validate bonus_eligibility logic for rep_summary
    Given a rep with total_rep_sales <total_rep_sales>
    When the pipeline calculates bonus_eligibility in rep_summary
    Then bonus_eligibility should be "<expected_eligibility>"

    Examples:
      | total_rep_sales | expected_eligibility |
      | 26000           | Yes                  |
      | 25001           | Yes                  |
      | 25000           | No                   |
      | 24999           | No                   |
      | 10000           | No                   |

  Scenario Outline: Validate rep_tier assignment in rep_summary
    Given a rep with total_rep_sales <total_rep_sales>
    When the pipeline calculates rep_tier
    Then rep_tier should be "<expected_tier>"

    Examples:
      | total_rep_sales | expected_tier   |
      | 50000           | Platinum Plus   |
      | 45001           | Platinum Plus   |
      | 45000           | Platinum        |
      | 40000           | Platinum        |
      | 35001           | Platinum        |
      | 35000           | Gold            |
      | 30000           | Gold            |
      | 25001           | Gold            |
      | 25000           | Silver          |
      | 10000           | Silver          |

  Scenario: Validate output DataFrame columns for kpi_df
    Given the pipeline has run with the updated logic
    When kpi_df is displayed
    Then the output should include columns:
      | transaction_id |
      | rep_name       |
      | product_name   |
      | sales_amount   |
      | sales_bucket   |
      | performance_flag |
      | rep_running_total |
      | sales_growth   |
      | rolling_avg_sales |
      | annual_rank    |
      | product_perf_band |

  Scenario: Validate output DataFrame columns for rep_summary
    Given the pipeline has run with the updated logic
    When rep_summary is displayed
    Then the output should include columns:
      | rep_id           |
      | rep_name         |
      | txn_count        |
      | total_rep_sales  |
      | avg_rep_sales    |
      | max_rep_sale     |
      | bonus_eligibility|
      | rep_tier         |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for missing or invalid sales_amount
    Given a sales transaction with sales_amount <sales_amount>
    When the pipeline processes the transaction
    Then an error "<expected_error>" should be raised

    Examples:
      | sales_amount | expected_error                       |
      | NULL         | "sales_amount is required"           |
      | "abc"        | "sales_amount must be numeric"       |
      | -100         | "sales_amount must be >= 0"          |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for duplicate transaction_id
    Given two sales transactions with the same transaction_id <transaction_id>
    When the pipeline processes the transactions
    Then an error "Duplicate transaction_id: <transaction_id>" should be raised

    Examples:
      | transaction_id |
      | TXN001         |
      | TXN999         |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for missing rep_id in rep_summary
    Given a rep_summary row with rep_id <rep_id>
    When the pipeline processes rep_summary
    Then an error "<expected_error>" should be raised

    Examples:
      | rep_id | expected_error           |
      | NULL   | "rep_id is required"     |

  Scenario: Validate allowed values for performance_flag
    Given the pipeline calculates performance_flag
    Then allowed values are "High", "Medium", "Low"
    And any other value should raise "Invalid performance_flag value"

  Scenario: Validate allowed values for product_perf_band
    Given the pipeline calculates product_perf_band
    Then allowed values are "Excellent", "Good", "Moderate", "Poor"
    And any other value should raise "Invalid product_perf_band value"

  Scenario: Validate allowed values for rep_tier
    Given the pipeline calculates rep_tier
    Then allowed values are "Platinum Plus", "Platinum", "Gold", "Silver"
    And any other value should raise "Invalid rep_tier value"

  Scenario: Validate bonus_eligibility values
    Given the pipeline calculates bonus_eligibility
    Then allowed values are "Yes", "No"
    And any other value should raise "Invalid bonus_eligibility value"

  Scenario: Validate type of total_rep_sales in rep_summary
    Given rep_summary is generated
    Then total_rep_sales must be numeric and >= 0

  Scenario: Validate type of sales_amount in kpi_df
    Given kpi_df is generated
    Then sales_amount must be numeric and >= 0

  Scenario: Validate display of final outputs
    Given the pipeline has run successfully
    When the final outputs are displayed
    Then kpi_df and rep_summary should reflect all updated logic and columns

# END
